1. Original MORIZON

MORIZON NEXT is based on the MORIZON forest zoning plugin distributed by
the Forestry Agency of Japan (林野庁) through the Geospatial Information
Center (geospatial.jp).

The original source package contains the following notice:

  ForestZoningPlugin
  Copyright (C) 2021 MIERUNE Inc.
  Contact stated in the original source: info@mierune.co.jp

The original MORIZON was developed through a project commissioned by the
Forestry Agency of Japan. The Japan Forest Technology Association
(日本森林技術協会) organized the zoning concept and workflow, and
MIERUNE Inc. implemented the QGIS plugin.

The file templates/sagyo_system_template_220113.xlsx is the unmodified
work-system spreadsheet template ("集材作業効率の設定220113.xlsx")
distributed in the ZoningKit data packages of the same MORIZON tool on
the official Forestry Agency distribution page. Only the file name has
been changed (to ASCII).

2. DEM source data and bundled indexes

MORIZON NEXT can download and process public VIRTUAL SHIZUOKA LP/Grid
DTM data published by Shizuoka Prefecture. The data itself is not
bundled in this plugin; it is downloaded from the public VIRTUAL
SHIZUOKA S3 distribution when the user selects that DEM source.

Source and project information:

  https://virtualshizuokaproject.my.canva.site/
  https://registry.opendata.aws/virtual_shizuoka/
  https://www.geospatial.jp/ckan/dataset/virtual-shizuoka-mw

The VIRTUAL SHIZUOKA public materials describe the data as open data
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). Some
catalog entries also mention Open Data Commons Open Database License
(ODbL). Users should confirm the current terms on the source data pages
when using the downloaded DEM data in outputs or redistribution.

The files dem_sources/data/nagano_sabo_dem_index.json and
dem_sources/data/nagano_rinmu_sheet_index.json are auxiliary index files
created for MORIZON NEXT.

nagano_sabo_dem_index.json was generated by inspecting the ZIP central
directories of the public Nagano Prefecture Construction Department
Sabo Division 0.5 m DEM dataset distributed through geospatial.jp:

  https://www.geospatial.jp/ckan/dataset/r3-4-50cmdem

nagano_rinmu_sheet_index.json was generated from the public index map
Shapefiles distributed with the Nagano Prefecture Forestry Department
0.5 m DEM dataset on geospatial.jp:

  https://www.geospatial.jp/ckan/dataset/nagano-dem

These index files contain tile-to-package or sheet-extent lookup data
only. They are used to select and download the necessary DEM tiles from
the public source datasets.

